Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.829 align:start position:0%
 
i'm the chairman of the nevada state  athletic commission  and i've announced that uh our  commission has launched an investigation  into the fraternity charity boxing event  that was held november 19 2021.  the nevada state athletic commission  takes this tragedy seriously  and our hearts go out to the valencia  valencia's family and loved ones  and as i've said we'll share further  details with you and answer questions  and that's the purpose of  this  press conference  uh i have been submitted questions by  many of you  and what i'd like to do because this is  very unusual uh i'm remote and most of  us are  i will read the question  and respond  as best as i can  as you know uh we have launched this  investigation  i have read certain things in the media  and until such time our commission  sees evidence  i will only speak about the evidence  that we have seen i will not  give you my personal opinion  the commission does not have a personal  opinion  and to be clear  the nevada state athletic commission  had no jurisdiction  for this event or any past events  that relate to this i would  say to you  please reference nrs section 467  with regard to the specificity of that  and we're here to speak of facts only  it had been reported by  metro  that nevada state athletic commission  has jurisdiction of this  we do not  we did not  for this event or any past events like  this  that doesn't mean after our  investigation that we may  have jurisdiction going forward  this is a tragedy  this is a homicide as the coroner  expressed  this is  an event that metro needs to fully  investigate as a homicide  and that's up to those that may or may  not prosecute  this homicide  with regard to our investigation we will  look at every aspect of this event  from what i've read  the wane occurred at unlv's student  union  the fraternities  under the auspices of unlv  the president the chancellor of those  universities and of course the board of  regents  they all have some explaining to do  so with that  i'm going to read questions that have  been submitted answer them to my best of  my ability  and i can tell you that in the past  we've done  some research at the nevada state  athletic commission  and uh  these types of events have happened in  in our state and other states  and uh i can tell you that  the athletic commission pursuant to  nevada revised statutes just doesn't  have authority yet as of yet  the outcome of this investigation will  be as i said based on evidence  if any wrongdoing is found  the enforcement of those actions  will be  handled pursuant to state laws  and of course  what has occurred in the county  it's been asked whether or not this  event was  permitted i don't know  a good question we will find out  that's a county business licensing issue  with regard to  having proper paramedics and medical  personnel  which nevada state athletic commission  would have liked to see  we did not sanction this  but they should have had proper  paramedics  and medical personnel at the event  with regard to the referee again we  don't know  we must find out  if this referee's ever been licensed  i've heard various reports that  the referee was acting a certain way we  don't know and can't be conclusive of  any of this but we will find out  also the students  were there proper matches between them  made  we don't know  but we will find out  were the students under the influence of  alcohol drugs  we don't know  but we will find out  so  i hope that answers some of your  questions  um  and  let me just go through please  all these questions that are being sent  to me right now in a very very  unorthodox way  um  so the question is if we have no  jurisdiction  how are we investigating that's an  interesting point if i led you to  believe we have no jurisdiction  uh  we did not have the ability to sanction  this event  but we do have the ability to  investigate  this event this event and that's what  we're  saying  um  fox 5 maddie white says people who  attended the event alleged medical  personnel were not on the scene during  the event  uh  i don't know that to be true or  untrue  so  a lot of the questions that you are uh  sending to us  they're they're great  and we will be extremely responsive  transparent and forthright with the  media  and all inquiries  uh the new york times  christine chung says  if  n-a-n-n-s-a-c doesn't have jurisdiction  i i apologize i'm a little dyslexic so  it's tough for me to read uh what is the  reason for an sac an investigation no we  do  have the ability to launch an  investigation christine  which we're doing  and  what was was  what is  has become a tragedy  what shall be in the future is most  important  to  investigate this situation and remedy it  and make  nevada the gold standard going forward a  better place a safer place  um  questions are still coming in so  we have not reviewed any footage of the  event i've not seen it  with regard to charity events being  required to have permits i can only  speak to the state level and i refer you  to nrs section 467  with regard to  the county permitting it with regard to  the university  having knowledge of this and accepting  and allowing this well go speak with the  university and the board of regents they  got a lot of explaining to do in my  opinion  um they cannot duck hide bob and weave  on this  and uh we're here to uncover the facts  the evidence  that  supports those facts  and be transparent with all of you  uh  let me see we still have questions  coming in thank you uh  so  maddie white of fox5 local  asked what's  our plan the commission  with regard to added oversight  for an approval process going forward  matt that's a very good question and  that's why we've launched an  investigation  to then to review the evidence  based on what we we find  determined the unfortunate circumstances  of what went wrong here and improve  uh  this approval process or sanctioning  process going forward  uh and i can't comment on that right now  i have some personal opinions but  i promise you that our commission will  do a thorough job will be transparent  and that we will come up with  a solution  going forward and when we do uh  an announcement will  be forthcoming with regard to how we  would like to handle this but it's going  to debate it's going to require debate  discussion amongst the commission  after we look at the facts  are there any other questions  this is this is interesting doing this  blind but  i'm going to ask are there any more  questions from the media  i will promise you that the nevada state  athletic commission will again be  transparent forthright  and  will hold  future  press  conferences as we gain facts  and it will be extremely cooperative and  i hope  that those that we ask  evidence from  are forthright  again this is a tragedy  our hearts go out to the valencia family  this is unnecessary  it shouldn't have happened  and that's why we have the nevada state  athletic commission because combat  sports  are just that  it's not a joke  serious  and that it takes this very seriously  with regard to that life safety and  health of those that combat within the  state  so with that i'll close this press  conference if there any questions please  send them  to the nevada state athletic commission  frankie mason within our offices  shall be your point person for that  and will come directly to me as the  chairman  of the nevada state athletic commission  thank you very much for your time this  morning  have a good day happy holidays

